I made three prompt edits to `out/main-B.workflow.json`, and the file still loads with python3. I didn't touch the start code node or the account post_process_code, didn't save to Freya, and didn't re-run any tests, so none of these fixes has been confirmed by a call yet.

- **His sister offers tomorrow evening (no callback scheduled): fixed.** This failure was real. With "now" on Wednesday 14 October, Thursday 15 October at 19:00 is the next business day and inside the 10:00–19:00 window, so the brief requires a callback. The agent turned it down anyway and kept asking. The callback prompt now says to check the second offered time against the allowed callback days, that exactly 10:00 and 19:00 count as inside, and to schedule it straight away without asking again or suggesting a time.
- **Pressure for an unauthorized exception (notes and a second close after the call was closed): fixed.** This failure was real: the agent closed the call and then tried to add notes and close again. The negotiate prompt's end step now says to add every note first, that close_call is the very last tool, and that no tool may be called after it.
- **One promise, one payment claim, one dispute (no promise recorded): fixed.** This failure was real, because Brief B rule 9 says a dispute or "already paid" claim on one product doesn't end the call. The agent went into the dispute/already-paid situations, which can't record promises, so it refused the card promise. The router prompt now sends a claim that covers only some products to negotiate, where the claim is noted and a promise can still be taken for the other products. It only goes to dispute or already-paid when the claim covers every product.

